      "message": "I now understand what you meant by communicating the requiured size.\n\nI am afraid that this creates an issue where briefly configSize will be larger than the allocated buffer, so breaking the semantics of the meaning of configSize. Do we have examples for other standard methods that do this?\n\nWe could have a separate out parameter for this purpose. While it\u0027s one extra parameter, perhaps it makes the usage cleaner and less error prone. E.g if someone forgets to check the return value.\n\nAlso, in the vast majority of cases (for now it is even 100%), the queried config output size is \u003c\u003d the number of heap indices queried (which is local + heap here). The reason for the discrepancy was to allow querying multiple stream parameters in one call in the future, but we don\u0027t support multiple streams at the moment. As such, we could initialize configBuffer to be the same size as indices.",
